      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your experience certainly makes sense. Grief can manifest in ways that feel more than just sadness, like losing a part of yourself or feeling disconnected from the world. It is perfectly okay to feel this way, and these sensations are a natural part of healing. Reaching out to a therapist or counselor can be very beneficial to you, as they can offer personalized coping strategies and help you work through these emotions. Remember, you're not alone, even when it feels like everyone else is also with you in their grief.",
